+ARM async guidance requires support for ≥4KB Location/AsyncOperation URLs and permissions beyond exact resource scope; actual path/region/provider operation read mapping remains Stage 7. Proposed permitted paths are exact job execution resources plus returned `Microsoft.App/locations/{selectedRegion}/containerappsjoboperationstatuses/{operationId}` or `...containerappsjoboperationresults/{operationId}` under accepted subscription, subject to verification of selected-version actual response. No arbitrary path/token forwarding is approved. General docs describe provider-varying status payloads; failed guessed reference URLs do not prove API absence. [ARM async](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-resource-manager/management/async-operations).
+
+## All seven execution states
+
+The selected GET documentation's meaning column merely repeats each enum label. Policy below is deliberately conservative; message/reason/endTime/container exit codes alone cannot override exact status or missing durable result.
+
+| State | Documented meaning | Policy | Stage 7 check |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Running | Running | Continue bounded observation | Exact GET and unchanged correlation |
+| Processing | Processing | Continue bounded observation | Demonstrate processing transition/handling |
+| Succeeded | Succeeded | Candidate success only with matching durable success | Missing/contradictory/mismatched result fails |
+| Failed | Failed | Failed; replay only if positively confirmed transient under one-replay contract | Failed durable evidence and classified replay |
+| Stopped | Stopped | Unsuccessful; no automatic transient inference | Stop receipt and result handling |
+| Degraded | Degraded | Uncertain, never passing or replay authorization | Selected-version behavior and conservative handling |
+| Unknown | Unknown | Uncertain/execution_unknown; operator recovery | Unknown handling, no second launch |
+
+Unrecognized enum, unavailable GET or observation deadline cannot pass; none authorizes transient replay. [Exact state schema](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/rest/api/resource-manager/containerapps/job-execution/job-execution?view=rest-resource-manager-containerapps-2026-07-01).
+
+## Tools and retry rationale
+
+Owner-accepted R3 deployment tool prerequisite contract: Azure CLI 2.90.0, Bicep CLI 0.38.33. CLI 2.90.0 and uv 0.12.15 were locally observed by root; Bicep and Docker/buildx are absent. Selected future method is ACR quick tasks on the D-05 dedicated Basic registry, Linux amd64 and exact Task 4 base/hashlock. Official releases demonstrate published versions, not local installation, API compatibility or build/publication success. Before later deployment, verify exact versions and Bicep build/type diagnostics without API-version substitution; any future build/publication requires separate action authorization/budget and digest proof. No installation or additional compute authorized here. [CLI release](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cli/azure/release-notes-azure-cli), [Bicep release](https://github.com/Azure/bicep/releases/tag/v0.38.33).
+
+Microsoft recommends at least one native retry for long-running replicas interrupted by maintenance. Accepted parent policy stays zero native retries because orchestration must distinguish confirmed failures from ambiguous launches and centrally limit replay; durable source worksets preserve resumable progress. This is a trade-off: a maintenance-interrupted replica can leave work incomplete, and zero retries is no maintenance guarantee. This disclosure requires review with the finding, not a redundant acceptance gate for the already accepted default; Stage 7 must retain maintenance/failure recovery and one-replay evidence. The recommendation and policy coexist without silently revising either. [Maintenance guidance](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/container-apps/jobs).

