## specs/evidence/sec-filing-index-ingestion/stage-1/source-assessment.md
Bytes: 13118; SHA-256: fef24f9a127fd14e364df25fd8778abfb9e6615a730dac1231036b97fff67cff
--- before/specs/evidence/sec-filing-index-ingestion/stage-1/source-assessment.md
+++ after/specs/evidence/sec-filing-index-ingestion/stage-1/source-assessment.md
@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+# Bounded source assessment
+
+Task 3 investigates filing indexes only. Root is the sole SEC issuer; this task performs offline inspection of its retained identity response bodies. The pinned end quarter is 2026Q4. Actual-child selection covers the earliest intended quarter 2010Q1, development start 2015Q1, latest closed 2026Q3, open 2026Q4 and root ZIP relationship; daily 2026-09-30/2026-10-01 cover the closed/open transition and handoff, 2026-10-02 is already published, and 2025-12-31/2026-01-02 cover the year transition. The planned matrix is ten receipt specimens, reusing the handoff for the transition role. The first daily receipt exposed a distinct selected text family, and root paused acquisition. Owner accepted the exact bounded daily-family continuation at 2026-10-06T00:00:39.782687Z, retaining the original 00:25:28Z deadline, original shared caps, four remaining daily URLs and at most 20 further attempts from count 146. Complete daily investigation resumed only after that acceptance. `specimens/matrix.json` records each receipt, listing provenance and actual URL. All ten actual-child receipts are complete. No absent required boundary was substituted and no new sampling allowance was inferred.
+
+## Originals, receipts and archive guards
+
+Original archives are retained as `<original-sha256>.zip`. Plain daily sources are retained as `<original-sha256>.idx`. Decoded ZIP members are separate `<decoded-sha256>.decoded.idx` derivatives. The acquisition `listings/SEC-*.body` files also remain immutable. Root/QTR4 receipts may share a hash-named file because their exact original bytes match; each receipt retains independent validators and provenance.
+
+Root's acquisition helper sends `Accept-Encoding: identity` and uses `http.client` without transparent entity decompression. It removes HTTP transfer framing, which is not source content, and retains the actual response entity bytes. Each inspection report records advertised Content-Length and equality where advertised; unadvertised length remains explicitly absent. Receipt sidecars link status, UTC receipt, User-Agent, MIME type, validators, byte count, digest, full response headers and immutable request intent. Content-Length, directory labels, source header dates and observed filing-date bounds remain separate facts. Only successful selected identity bodies enter this assessment; no error/HTML/truncated body is treated as a specimen.
+
+Each ZIP is opened offline. Exactly one member named `master.idx` is required before any extraction; unexpected names (including traversal/absolute paths), extra members, encryption and declared expansion above 512 MiB are rejected. Streaming extraction into a unique `/private/tmp/sec-edgar-task3-*` directory checks actual bytes against that cap and declared size; Python ZIP streaming reads validate member CRC. The temporary directory is removed after inspection. The derivative is then retained separately. Reports record member name, ZIP codec number, compressed/expanded bytes, CRC32, flags, actual expansion and hash. Codec 8 is ZIP DEFLATE. Integrity operations exited 0 for the retained archives. No extraction enters package paths.
+
+The offline synthetic guard check covers traversal names, absolute names, excess members, a lowered expansion cap and strict-decoder rejection. It is investigation-tool verification, not golden source/parser evidence. A later annotation-helper defect required a scoped red/green repair: quarterly fields were wrongly applied to the distinct daily CSV schema. The direct CSV writer stopped after 2,172 rows; four tail rows were recovered from immutable SEC-0138/0139 children. The helper now uses daily outcome/evidence columns and writes to a temporary file before atomic replacement. A complete comparison against the frozen Task 2 review diff verifies all 2,176 original daily rows and all 372 quarterly rows in original order, with no original field changes except authorized selected status/reason annotations. The first synthetic regression fixture missed the SEC-* filename glob and failed; its stdout/stderr were subsequently overwritten. Exact original failure bytes are not separately retained, and this loss is explicit in annotation-repair-sequence.json. Corrected pre-fix algorithm reproduction exits 1 with the schema ValueError; actual corrected code exits 0. The initial fixture failure is not recreated as original evidence. The first daily inspection deliberately failed at the unknown quarterly header guard; its initial failure command/output remain retained.
+
+## Selected format and path observations
+
+`specimens/SEC-*.inspection.json` records complete scans of every nonempty post-header row in each retained body, rather than a few-row format inference. Reports retain header lines, representative raw rows and split fields, counts, source date bounds and decoding evidence. All fully inspected quarterly rows have the exact header `CIK|Company Name|Form Type|Date Filed|Filename`; daily rows have `CIK|Company Name|Form Type|Date Filed|File Name`. Both have pipe separators, five fields and `edgar/data/<CIK>/<10 digits>-<2 digits>-<6 digits>.txt` paths. All retained text decodes strictly as ASCII, with no BOM or high bytes; no lossy replacement was used. Quarterly derivatives have CRLF endings. Inspected daily sources have LF endings, with exact counts per receipt in the matrix. Filing dates were checked with `date.fromisoformat`; quarterly dates are YYYY-MM-DD and daily dates are YYYYMMDD. Lexical extrema are valid date extrema within each fixed-width observed form. Daily 2026-09-30 includes filing dates from 2025-08-25 through 2026-09-30. Filename/header date cannot be a Date Filed filter; raw earlier dates and representative date-bound rows remain retained.
+
+The observed selected representation boundary is ZIP containing one DEFLATE `master.idx` member and uncompressed daily IDX, with the retained textual/path family above. The daily family was discovered as a novelty: SEC-0146 first 2 KiB revealed File Name rather than Filename, compact YYYYMMDD dates and LF endings. `SEC-0146.novelty.json` preserves the bounded observation and original direct hash verification. Root stopped acquisition and obtained explicit owner continuation (`daily-family-continuation-acceptance.json`) before extending the offline observational helper. The initial failure receipts remain separate from `SEC-0146.dailyfamilyinspection*` success receipts. This is an investigation boundary and Task 4 input, not implementation support certification. Both selected families now have complete retained original-byte evidence and full bounded observations; all ten matrix receipts pass independent verification. Optional `.sit`, `.z`, `.Z`, `.gz` and daily ZIP/GZIP/compress alternatives remain unselected, unexamined and unsupported. The earliest intended 2010Q1 full scan found no additional legacy filename family. No non-extractable path or nullable accession example appeared in the retained matrix; their absence from these samples does not remove the parent nullable-accession requirement or establish global absence. No unexamined format/path family becomes supported by analogy. Later golden parser verification remains required, and the 33 uninspected historical daily middle quarters retain D-14's recovery limitation.
+
+The root and 2026Q4 original ZIP bytes and decoded member bytes are compared directly in the independent check, in addition to matching hashes. Receipt-time equality does not guarantee future equality or allow either URL to substitute for arbitrary quarter coverage. The open-quarter header says Last Data Received October 3, 2026 while observed rows end October 2; the header label does not add filing coverage.
+
+## Parent raw naming contract
+
+Parent §4.5's `master.idx` is an example, not permission to store decoded content as original bytes. This investigation's hash-plus-original-extension names preserve the original format; receipt metadata retains the actual URL/extension and separate derivative path. This is local evidence naming and does not propose a durable production naming contract change. Production raw naming must retain original archive bytes and format metadata when ZIP is selected. No accepted contract revision or owner acceptance is needed for keeping evidence originals and derivatives separate; no production naming decision is asserted here.
+
+## Volume and temporary space
+
+`specimens/volume-assessment.json` sums the 68 requested quarterly child labels by representation; the root bridge is excluded from range-volume totals to avoid counting the open quarter twice. Optional representation totals describe alternatives and must not be added into a mandatory download estimate. KB/MB/GB labels are retained as labeled totals; any binary scaling to planning bytes is an explicit unverified 1024-based assumption. Rounded directory labels are not received-byte measurements. Largest listed ZIP and largest retained source are recorded separately. Archive expansion ratios come from actual original and expanded bytes. Retained file lengths and original/derivative totals are measurements; directory allocation is not used as expansion evidence.
+
+The one-source model is the largest observed original plus its expanded derivative plus the scratch/reserve terms below: 1,192,636,112 bytes. A separate co-resident-sample illustration totals 1,258,200,083 bytes from 13,425,383 measured unique original bytes and 84,787,910 measured unique derivative bytes plus the same scratch/reserve assumptions. The co-resident temporary-peak model is simultaneous retained unique originals + their expanded derivatives + planned observation/output scratch + candidate-generation scratch + installer/runtime/log reserve. The first two terms are measured retained file lengths. Observation/output scratch assumes one largest observed expanded source, candidate-generation scratch assumes twice that source, and installer/runtime/log reserve assumes 1 GiB. These assumptions are planning allowances, not measured process scratch. The retained matrix is small; the largest observed source/ratio is not a tail bound for all 68 quarters. Uninspected bodies may differ in encoding, rows, expansion or size, and unknown listing-size labels remain explicit.
+
+The retained Microsoft documentation `provider/preparation/20261005T230634Z/storage-mounts.web-extract.txt`, lines 44–53, states over 1 vCPU has 8 GiB ephemeral storage per replica. Candidate 2 vCPU therefore maps to documented 8 GiB temporary capacity. This task used only the previously retained documentation and did not perform fresh provider retrieval; provider freshness and integrated effective behavior remain Task 5/7 questions. The bounded measured-plus-assumed model is compared with that documented capacity in the JSON. It is not a measured 4 GiB-memory or 3,600-second-runtime fit. No blocking documented disk incompatibility or setting revision is inferred from this sample model.
+
+Recommend processing one selected source unit at a time with the existing 512 MiB per-specimen investigation expansion bound, inspecting declared members/size before extraction, and releasing local scratch after the unit is durably retained. This is a bounded investigation recommendation, not worker design. Any over-cap source, new selected format/path family, or required expanded sampling must pause acquisition for root coordination and accepted continuation; these ten samples do not authorize expanding the original window or twelve-specimen cap.
+
+## Verification and limits
+
+Exact local inspection commands, stdout, stderr and exit codes are retained alongside each inspection. `source-verification-command.json` and its stdout/stderr retain the final independent receipt/hash/CRC/full-row/date/matrix and root/QTR equality check. Direct `shasum -a 256` output verifies every distinct original and derivative. `offline-guard-command.json` retains the synthetic guard check. No production parser, catalog, ingestion tests, package repair, infrastructure definitions, provisioning or runtime probes were created by this task. Stage 1 readiness remains a root/owner decision.
+
+The daily filing-date observations affect prior output quarters: under parent §4.3 retain and validate supported original indexes, under the canonical row contract the valid filing date determines the output quarter, and under §4.4 preserve observations and apply quarterly precedence/approved-withdrawal rules to each affected quarter. A daily filename is a source period, not a constraint that every row has that filing date. Absence from an open snapshot cannot authorize deletion; old daily observations cannot undo an approved closed-quarter replacement. These are existing-contract implications, not new publication authority or implemented parser behavior.
+
+Across all listed alternatives, the largest labeled body is 2026Q1 `master.idx`, 32,282 KB. It is unselected/unfetched; its label is not an expanded-byte measurement. The largest retained expansion remains 28,748,322 bytes, reinforcing that the sample maximum is not a full-range bound.

